.TH LINUX-MONITOR 1 "September 2026" "linux-monitor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-monitor \- lightweight Linux desktop performance monitor overlay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-monitor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linux-monitor
is a native, lightweight Linux performance overlay that directly samples system metrics
from /proc, /sys and NVIDIA NVML without spawning external shell processes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-session\fR
Print detected display server / desktop session information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-config\fR
Print currently loaded configuration and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-window\fR
Sample metrics once, print output to stdout, and exit.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/linux-monitor/config.toml
.RS
User configuration file.
.RE
